ides a quick overview of seven architecture patterns (layered, microservices, event-driven, micro kernel, serverless, space-based, hexagonal) with guidance on when to use or avoid each. The core message: simplicity enables scale, not the other way around.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/bNKRiN86cho/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":4,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-05-07T15:30:16.000Z"},{"id":"T6ajXwE6e","title":"AI Automation: The Unreliable Trap & Why Humans Are Key! #shorts","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Ei5R3porJEU","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/ai-automation-the-unreliable-trap-why-humans-are-key-shorts-t6ajxwe6e","summary":null,"image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/Ei5R3porJEU/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-05-05T12:00:31.000Z"},{"id":"36lPEDu4i","title":"Boost Your System Speed & Slash Costs Effortlessly! #shorts","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=No-kqjGA0eU","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/boost-your-system-speed-slash-costs-effortlessly-shorts-36lpedu4i","summary":null,"image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/No-kqjGA0eU/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-05-05T08:01:24.000Z"},{"id":"48xMPuaGR","title":"SQL Server Downtime: Hackers, Upgrades & Inevitable Chaos! #shorts","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=KFbcuzTmj0Y","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/sql-server-downtime-hackers-upgrades-inevitable-chaos-shorts-48xmpuagr","summary":null,"image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/KFbcuzTmj0Y/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-05-05T03:59:32.000Z"},{"id":"MkyOKqhq6","title":"AI Isn't Perfect: Why I Don't Trust It! #shorts","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LRjWwvtdt2E","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/ai-isn-t-perfect-why-i-don-t-trust-it-shorts-mkyokqhq6","summary":null,"image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/LRjWwvtdt2E/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-05-04T23:54:25.000Z"},{"id":"y5vlc0yMp","title":"Coding Made Easy: Smart Actors Handle Failures Automatically! #shorts","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=vAJp9NljAyY","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/coding-made-easy-smart-actors-handle-failures-automatically-shorts-y5vlc0ymp","summary":null,"image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/vAJp9NljAyY/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-05-04T19:56:27.000Z"},{"id":"KWeoFxWhW","title":"Unlock Speed: Actors Eliminate Race Conditions for Lockless Systems! #shorts","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=kg842yjtKVU","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/unlock-speed-actors-eliminate-race-conditions-for-lockless-systems-shorts-kweofxwhw","summary":null,"image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/kg842yjtKVU/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-05-04T16:03:39.000Z"},{"id":"CVG0S6EDU","title":"Unlock True Parallelism: 8 Cores for Lightning-Fast Actor Processing! #shorts","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=TjYFFlRAqf4","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/unlock-true-parallelism-8-cores-for-lightning-fast-actor-processing-shorts-cvg0s6edu","summary":null,"image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/TjYFFlRAqf4/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-05-04T13:33:39.000Z"},{"id":"EIQdt17pF","title":"Powerful Systems Run on Cheaper Hardware: No More Corrupt Data! #shorts","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=I0q68k99Jpo","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/powerful-systems-run-on-cheaper-hardware-no-more-corrupt-data-shorts-eiqdt17pf","summary":null,"image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/I0q68k99Jpo/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-05-04T07:59:23.000Z"},{"id":"9ibUIDyhV","title":"AI is an Intern: Can We EVER Trust It? #shorts","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=19wWXUD4HXY","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/ai-is-an-intern-can-we-ever-trust-it-shorts-9ibuidyhv","summary":null,"image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/19wWXUD4HXY/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2026-05-04T03:59:21.000Z"}],"top_posts":[{"id":"Kh4oLamRJ","title":"Why startups should stop chasing uptime nines and focus on recovery speed","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1JCJ7cOIvSs","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/11-reliability-principles-every-cto-learns-too-late-kh4olamrj","summary":"A pragmatic take on reliability engineering for startups, arguing that chasing high uptime targets (99.99%+) is an exponential cost trap that kills velocity before product-market fit. Key principles include: each additional nine of uptime costs 10x more in engineering overhead; resume-driven development (Kubernetes, microservices, multi-region) wastes millions solving imaginary scale problems; modular monoliths outperform premature microservices; high-availability automation itself caused AWS's 14-hour outage; boring technology is a strategic advantage since LLMs have better training data for it; error budgets replace the speed-vs-stability debate with objective data; and the maintenance ratio (50-80% of mature system costs) crushes delivery throughput. The core mindset shift: reliability is about recovery speed, not uptime percentage. A team deploying 10x/day that recovers in 5 minutes beats a complex self-healing system nobody understands. Exceptions exist for fintech, healthcare, and telecom where reliability is the product itself.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/1JCJ7cOIvSs/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":124,"num_comments":3,"created_at":"2026-04-10T21:29:31.000Z"},{"id":"Krs1a6lDO","title":"Take ownership of your career instead of waiting for permission","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yP-UX6zROV4","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/stop-waiting-no-one-s-coming-the-hard-truth-that-saved-my-career--krs1a6ldo","summary":"A developer shares their 30-year journey from corporate stagnation to career ownership, arguing that waiting for recognition or permission is futile. The core message: stop blaming external factors, take ownership of your career, document your wins, create your own opportunities, and invest in yourself. Practical advice includes keeping track of achievements, writing unsolicited proposals to demonstrate capability, and building systems that drive progress regardless of title or approval.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/yP-UX6zROV4/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":63,"num_comments":10,"created_at":"2025-11-27T16:35:25.000Z"},{"id":"TgCfn0diP","title":"Seven behavioral patterns that distinguish advancing developers from stagnant ones","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bWH7Fnzv50c","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/7-signs-you-re-a-stuck-developer-and-how-senior-engineers-break-free--tgcfn0dip","summary":"Seven behavioral patterns distinguish developers who advance from those who stagnate: taking initiative without permission, working around obstacles instead of complaining, documenting achievements systematically, admitting knowledge gaps confidently, measuring progress against past self rather than peers, curating relationships that support growth, and taking ownership instead of blaming external factors. Each pattern is actionable through specific weekly practices like maintaining a brag document, proposing solutions proactively, and auditing time spent with colleagues.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/bWH7Fnzv50c/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":52,"num_comments":5,"created_at":"2025-12-18T17:10:32.000Z"},{"id":"i4b4dZpQb","title":"Three warning signs you're stagnating as a developer","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=GnfNN6aZkJA","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/3-signs-you-re-falling-behind-as-a-developer-and-don-t-see-it-yet--i4b4dzpqb","summary":"Three warning signs indicate career stagnation: becoming defensive about feedback instead of learning from it, spending most time on maintenance and firefighting rather than building new things, and avoiding learning technologies that feel intimidating. The solution involves actively seeking feedback, automating repetitive work to free up time for growth projects, and deliberately learning new skills that push you outside your comfort zone.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/GnfNN6aZkJA/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":35,"num_comments":4,"created_at":"2026-02-05T16:59:58.000Z"},{"id":"1yFH35yf1","title":"Seven career mistakes developers make that prevent advancement","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Mg0xgU7dL7g","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/7-career-mistakes-i-d-avoid-if-i-started-coding-again-cto-advice--1yfh35yf1","summary":"A CTO with 40 years of experience shares seven career mistakes to avoid: being too helpful instead of strategic, failing to document and communicate achievements, not speaking the language of business metrics, avoiding organizational politics, staying too long in toxic cultures, focusing solely on technical skills over positioning, and not building external credibility. The advice emphasizes that career advancement requires strategic thinking, visibility management, business acumen, and deliberate self-promotion rather than just technical excellence.","image":"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/Mg0xgU7dL7g/sddefault.jpg","num_upvotes":41,"num_comments":2,"created_at":"2026-01-08T16:53:00.000Z"}],"similar_handles":["webtechie","dereuromark","stepsecurity","simondev758","java-oracle"],"opposite_handles":["horde","dailydevworld","watercooler","on_leuwcq","dotnetsquad"],"similar":[{"id":"webtechie","handle":"webtechie","name":"WebTechie","is_squad":false,"x":-4.6262,"y":-6.3199,"cluster_id":1,"posts_collected":97,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/s--Q98Q0_9X--/f_auto,q_auto/v1774960848/logos/webtechie?_a=BAMAMiWQ0","features_preview":{"posts_per_week":30.935806,"median_upvotes":0.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"hype_score":0.0,"avg_read_time":4.041237,"tag_diversity":0.57732},"top_tags_preview":[["java",80],["raspber